// BUG (found 2026-10-16): `String + String` fails on the LLVM backend.
//
// Reproducer:
//
//     proc main()
//         print("hello" + " world")
//
// produces:
//
//     error[E0009]: codegen: Add received non-numeric operands
//                   (left=ptr, right=ptr) — builder should have coerced
//     error[E0002]: Codegen failed: ...
//
// Confirmed pre-existing by checking out commit 1cbd370 (origin/main
// at the time this was discovered): same error, same shape.
//
// Likely location: `src/backends/llvm_codegen/binop.rs` or the IR
// builder's string-add lowering. `Add` should lower to
// `algol26_string_concat`, not to LLVM `add`. The diagnostic message
// "builder should have coerced" names the fault as upstream of the
// LLVM backend.
//
// This file is NOT run by `adr_examples_runner` because that runner
// stops at CFG dataflow, before LLVM codegen. It exists as a
// documentation reproducer. Move it under tests/adr_examples/ and
// mark EXPECT: COMPILE once the codegen path is fixed and the runner
// is extended to cover it.
proc main()
    print("hello" + " world")
